\title{Folding, Recursion, and Aggregation}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    How a proof about a long computation is assembled from proofs about short ones. Every zkVM that
    proves a real workload is doing this, and it is where the soundness argument becomes hardest to
    keep track of — the [Nova bug](dhsorens-003M) is the standing example.
}

